# Pioneer DJ / AlphaTheta controllers — grant the logged-in user access to the
# HID interface.
#
# Why this is needed: rekordbox identifies a connected controller through the
# Windows HID stack (HidD_GetHidGuid / SetupDiEnumDeviceInterfaces /
# HidD_GetAttributes), not through MIDI. Wine's winebus.sys enumerates HID
# devices from /dev/hidraw*, which is root-only by default, so under Wine the
# controller is invisible to that path. rekordbox then never binds the device
# and never opens its MIDI port — the controller sits in its power-on LED
# animation and no control does anything.
#
# TAG+="uaccess" gives the active seat's user an ACL on the node, which is the
# same mechanism game controllers use. No group membership required.
#
# The 60- prefix is load-bearing: systemd acts on the uaccess tag in
# /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/73-seat-late.rules, so a rule numbered above 73 adds the
# tag too late and no ACL is ever granted. This file was first written as 99-
# and silently did nothing.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2b73", MODE="0660", GROUP="audio", TAG+="uaccess"
